{
  "phase": "train",
  "version": 2,
  "items": [
    {
      "id": "s0001",
      "text": "When a clue describes a relational trope, search broadly across genres rather than assuming romance-only",
      "created_by": "merge",
      "ts": "2026-10-16T19:34:28+08:00",
      "total_score": 2,
      "rating_count": 3,
      "source_ids": [
        "s0001"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0002",
      "text": "When clues include relocation, early writing age, and a degree, prioritize famous authors with documented biographies before niche matches",
      "created_by": "merge",
      "ts": "2026-10-16T19:34:28+08:00",
      "total_score": 2,
      "rating_count": 3,
      "source_ids": [
        "s0002"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0005",
      "text": "Run retrieval searches before composing any answer; never draft a response from memory alone",
      "created_by": "merge",
      "ts": "2026-10-16T19:34:28+08:00",
      "total_score": 2,
      "rating_count": 1,
      "source_ids": [
        "s0005",
        "t1.2.2.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0013",
      "text": "When initial clue matches point to one genre, semantically describe the full combined plot in one query before drilling into specifics",
      "created_by": "merge",
      "ts": "2026-10-16T19:34:28+08:00",
      "total_score": 2,
      "rating_count": 3,
      "source_ids": [
        "s0013"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0015",
      "text": "Decompose the clue into discrete verifiable attributes and run one parallel search per attribute before merging",
      "created_by": "merge",
      "ts": "2026-10-16T19:34:28+08:00",
      "total_score": 2,
      "rating_count": 1,
      "source_ids": [
        "t1.2.2.1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0016",
      "text": "Rank clues by discriminative power and anchor on the rarest one first to enumerate candidates before chasing memorable details",
      "created_by": "merge",
      "ts": "2026-10-16T19:34:28+08:00",
      "total_score": 2,
      "rating_count": 1,
      "source_ids": [
        "t1.2.3.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0003",
      "text": "When asked for a specific name, search famous literary characters whose role is replaced by a protagonist in classic novels",
      "created_by": "merge",
      "ts": "2026-10-16T19:34:28+08:00",
      "total_score": 1,
      "rating_count": 3,
      "source_ids": [
        "s0003"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0004",
      "text": "For author-biographical clues about a pioneer parent, search the author's own biography and family page before inferring from plot",
      "created_by": "merge",
      "ts": "2026-10-16T19:34:28+08:00",
      "total_score": 1,
      "rating_count": 1,
      "source_ids": [
        "s0004"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0008",
      "text": "Fully read all high-relevance semantic search results before drawing conclusions, even when lexical results seem more authoritative",
      "created_by": "merge",
      "ts": "2026-10-16T19:34:28+08:00",
      "total_score": 1,
      "rating_count": 1,
      "source_ids": [
        "s0008"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0009",
      "text": "After locating a candidate publication title in a snippet, re-search the corpus verbatim to verify exact wording before answering",
      "created_by": "merge",
      "ts": "2026-10-16T19:34:28+08:00",
      "total_score": 1,
      "rating_count": 3,
      "source_ids": [
        "s0009"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0010",
      "text": "Once a primary entity and its affiliate are confirmed, pivot to a related entity linked by family or professional ties and search their attributes jointly",
      "created_by": "merge",
      "ts": "2026-10-16T19:34:28+08:00",
      "total_score": 1,
      "rating_count": 3,
      "source_ids": [
        "s0010"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0012",
      "text": "When one regional hypothesis stalls on a key clue, pivot early to alternative regions rather than deepening the same branch",
      "created_by": "merge",
      "ts": "2026-10-16T19:34:28+08:00",
      "total_score": 1,
      "rating_count": 1,
      "source_ids": [
        "s0012"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0014",
      "text": "Before committing to a hypothesis, run a sanity-check search for the presumed answer's title or author to falsify the guess",
      "created_by": "merge",
      "ts": "2026-10-16T19:34:28+08:00",
      "total_score": 1,
      "rating_count": 1,
      "source_ids": [
        "s0014"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0017",
      "text": "Test every clue against the top candidate and re-search any that don't fit rather than dismissing mismatches",
      "created_by": "merge",
      "ts": "2026-10-16T19:34:28+08:00",
      "total_score": 1,
      "rating_count": 1,
      "source_ids": [
        "t1.2.3.1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0007",
      "text": "When retrieved sources conflict on a key fact, investigate both rather than defaulting to the most familiar source",
      "created_by": "merge",
      "ts": "2026-10-16T19:34:28+08:00",
      "total_score": 0,
      "rating_count": 3,
      "source_ids": [
        "s0007"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0006",
      "text": "When a question specifies source date and publication, treat exact wording as success criterion and verify it verbatim against the passage",
      "created_by": "merge",
      "ts": "2026-10-16T19:34:28+08:00",
      "total_score": -1,
      "rating_count": 3,
      "source_ids": [
        "s0006"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0011",
      "text": "Before finalizing, verify every distinctive claim against at least one independent source; persist only when multiple clues align",
      "created_by": "merge",
      "ts": "2026-10-16T19:34:28+08:00",
      "total_score": -2,
      "rating_count": 3,
      "source_ids": [
        "s0011"
      ]
    }
